  "scope": "All 37 owner-adopted success cases (originals-catalog.md A/B/C): what the owner hands over and the SHA-256 recorded for it. Metadata only: no original bytes are committed (the repository is public). Every sha256 here already appears in manifest.json, originals-index.json, originals-catalog.md or the case's CP-*.md record on develop. Every file name appears in those records too, except the two ZIP names marked name_source (SR-002, CP-033), recorded only on the unmerged PR #237 / #240 branches. Does not change manifest.json, second-root-research-successes.json or their counts, and does not widen the case-study counting rules (case-study.ts still reads only originals-index.json and manifest.json).",
  "rules": {
    "verified": "A provided file is an original only when its SHA-256 equals a sha256 in this file's request for that id (adopted originals). Other recorded SHA-256s (manifest.json viewing copies, drafts, comparison sheets; originals-index.json) are reported as recorded_not_original and never promote a case. A ZIP whose own SHA-256 is not in the request is 'verified via member': only its members whose SHA-256 is in the request are originals, the other members stay unverified. A ZIP's SHA256SUMS (when present) must match entirely.",
    "no_sha": "An entry whose sha256 is null can never be verified: a provided file stays unverified and is never registered as an original.",
    "pseudo": "Files the owner places under <id>/pseudo/ are pseudo-restorations: always labelled so, never registered as originals, whatever their SHA-256.",
    "private": "Originals stay outside the repository (docs/design/success-originals-handover.md)."
  },
